# Root build-context excludes (packaging work package, docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md
# §7 Phase 5, 2026-08-17). Only vault-api's build uses the repo root as its
# context (`docker build -f api/Dockerfile .`, deploy/compose.yaml's
# vault-api `build:` block) -- needed so `COPY web /app/web` in
# api/Dockerfile can reach web/, a repo-root SIBLING of api/, not a child of
# it. vault-core and vault-dns keep their OWN build contexts (../core, ../dns
# in deploy/compose.yaml) and never see this file at all -- Docker only
# applies a .dockerignore that lives at the root of the context being used.
#
# Without this file, that repo-root context would include the entire Android
# toolchain tree (app/), the Phase-0 PoC evidence trees (poc/), and every
# other component's own directory on every `docker build` -- none of it used
# by the vault-api image. MEASURED on this checkout (`docker build`'s own
# "Sending build context to Docker daemon" line, real WSL2/Docker 29.1.3,
# re-measured after the api/*.md /pytest.ini /requirements-dev.txt
# additions below): 9.734 MB without this file, 1.54 MB with it -- an 84%
# reduction, on a
# worktree checkout where `.git` is just a small link file, not the full
# object store, and where the Android tree has never actually been built
# (no populated Gradle cache under app/). A normal clone with a real `.git/`
# and a built `app/` would see a far bigger absolute reduction; the ~81%
# relative share this file removes is the number that carries over. None of
# the excludes below touch api/ or web/ (aside from web/tests/, which the
# image never serves) -- api/Dockerfile COPYs both of those in and needs
# them present.

# VCS and tooling metadata -- never part of a built image.
.git
.github
.claude

# Other components' own trees. core/ and dns/ build from their own
# directories (see the header note) so excluding them here costs vault-api's
# build nothing; agent/ (Go) and app/ (Android/Kotlin) are entirely unrelated
# runtimes; deploy/ is Compose/docs, not image content; docs/ and poc/ are
# documentation and throwaway PoC evidence.
app/
poc/
docs/
agent/
core/
dns/
deploy/

# Test trees -- not shipped, and web/tests/ specifically drags in a Node
# toolchain's worth of fixtures that have nothing to do with the served app
# shell. api/tests/ is pytest-only, already excluded from the image by
# api/Dockerfile only ever COPYing api/vault_api (never api/tests).
web/tests/
api/tests/

# api/'s own dev-only files -- carried over from the deleted api/.dockerignore
# so its "everything is folded in here" claim below is actually true.
# api/requirements-dev.txt in particular is not an oversight: api/Dockerfile
# spends a whole comment explaining that dev dependencies (pytest, httpx) are
# deliberately never installed in the image, and excluding the file this
# early keeps that decision visible instead of leaving an unused file sitting
# in the context for someone to wonder about. None of these three are ever
# COPYed by api/Dockerfile; excluding them only shrinks the context, it does
# not change what ships. api/README.md alone measured 302,992 bytes -- 16%
# of the 1.845 MB build context above -- so this is not a rounding-error
# cleanup.
api/*.md
api/pytest.ini
api/requirements-dev.txt

# Python bytecode / cache artifacts, wherever they exist in the tree. The
# `**/` prefix is load-bearing, not decoration: a bare `__pycache__/` (no
# `**/`) anchors at the CONTEXT ROOT only -- a lesson learned in review the
# first time this project had a Python build context, under api/'s own
# now-deleted `.dockerignore` (its rules, including this one, are folded in
# here; it is gone because Docker only reads a .dockerignore at the root of
# whatever context is actually in use, and that root moved to the repo root
# -- an api/-rooted build no longer even works, every COPY source in
# api/Dockerfile is repo-root-relative now). vault_api/__pycache__,
# vault_api/routers/__pycache__ etc. all need the recursive form or the
# exact same stale-bytecode bug reappears one directory level deeper.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/

# Local, uncommitted, or generated -- never valid build input. Same `**/`
# requirement as above: api/vault.db, a stray api/.env, etc. all live below
# the new context root, not at it. api/cache/ is what a native dev run's
# default VAULT_CACHE_ROOT ("./cache", relative to cwd) creates if uvicorn is
# ever launched from inside api/ -- carried over from the old api/-rooted
# .dockerignore, which excluded it for the same reason.
**/.venv/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/.env
api/cache/
